OSL-2.1 Open Software License v. 2.1
Can
Use/reproduce, Distribute, Modify/merge, Sublicense, Commercial use
Must
Incl. Copyright, State changes, Disclose source, Copyleft/Share a., Include licence
Cannot
Hold liable, Use trademark
Compatible
Linking freedom, For software
Law
Licensor's law, Not fixed/local, Venue fixed
Support
OSI approved, FSF Free/Libre

Licence comment:
Written by Lawrence Rosen (attorney, formal counsel of the Open Source Initiative), OSL is seen as a reciprocal licence, incompatible with the GPL. It is interoperable (freedom of linking with other software). Law and jurisdiction where Licensor resides or conducts its primary business.
